       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and they don't add much analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere are some options within the labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum daily dose.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common regimen for inflammatory conditions.\n\nYou may have meant a single dose of 1600 mg, or 1600 mg/day split into smaller doses, such as 400 mg four times daily. Tell me which you intended, or choose one of the options above, and I'll enter it right away. If the patient needs more analgesia than the maximum dose gives, I can also enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen."
      }
     ],
