       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here. The order is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day, so I treat the protocol as a claim and not as grounds to exceed that limit.\n\nThere are a few ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the limit now.** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can enter that immediately.\n- **Use a different route for a protocol-based exception.** If a real high-dose protocol exists, the pharmacy or an order set that supports an approved override can place the order. That route keeps the pharmacist's review and the monitoring in the record.\n- **Add other analgesia.** If the goal is more pain control, I can enter scheduled acetaminophen or another agent alongside ibuprofen.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
